# REPO-WIDE LINE-ENDING POLICY.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. An edit rewrote two source files CRLF and turned a 12-line change
# into a 2,862-line diff. Nothing caught it structurally -- no hash pin covered those files,
# and it surfaced only because the arithmetic in a receipt refused to reconcile. That is luck,
# not design. Before this file, `eol=lf` was declared in exactly ONE directory
# (docs/replay-results/h1-battery/.gitattributes) and nowhere else, so every other text file
# in the repo was one Windows-side write away from the same whole-file rewrite.
#
# MEASURED STATE AT THE TIME OF WRITING (`git ls-files --eol`, 4,267 tracked files):
#   4,098 blobs i/lf  |  4 blobs i/crlf  |  109 i/none (no EOL) |  56 i/-text (binary)
# The repo stores LF. The policy below states that fact so no checkout, clone, or
# `core.autocrlf` setting on another machine can reintroduce the translation.
#
# ★ THIS FILE DOES NOT NORMALIZE ANYTHING THAT ALREADY EXISTS. Declaring `text eol=lf` over a
# blob that is ALREADY stored CRLF makes git compare a normalized working tree against a CRLF
# blob, so the file reports as modified forever and the next `git add` commits a whole-file
# rewrite -- which is the exact defect this file exists to prevent. The four such blobs are
# therefore EXEMPTED BY NAME below rather than silently swept in. Measured: without the
# exemptions those four stage 7,902 insertions + 7,902 deletions (15,804 lines) of pure
# line-ending churn.
#
# ★ AND `git status` DOES NOT TELL YOU THIS BY ITSELF. On a fresh checkout it reported all
# four CLEAN -- not because they matched, but because git's stat cache had not been
# invalidated and nothing had looked. They only appeared after `touch` +
# `git update-index --really-refresh`. Clean because nothing has looked is not clean.
#
# THE FOUR EXEMPTED FILES ARE A DEFERRED NORMALIZATION UNIT -- their own change, with its own
# review. They are NOT fixed here, and they are NOT forgotten: scripts/check_line_ending_rewrite.py
# reports them under `--audit` so the debt stays visible instead of decaying into folklore.

*.py     text eol=lf
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.cjs    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.jsonl  text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts are deliberately NOT forced to LF: *.bat and *.cmd are read by
# cmd.exe, which has historically required CRLF, and *.ps1 is conventionally CRLF. Leaving
# them unspecified is a decision, not an omission.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# KNOWN-NONCONFORMING BLOBS -- stored CRLF in the object store TODAY. `!text !eol` leaves the
# attributes UNSPECIFIED for these paths, which is what keeps the working tree clean; `-text`
# would also work but would make git diff them as binary, and these are review artifacts that
# must stay readable in a diff. Normalizing them is a separate unit with its own review.
#
#   provenance -- all four entered the object store CRLF in these commits:
#     50d28edb  (not these paths; the 2,862-line instance, since normalized)
#     6fd36843  "restore: re-land AR-200..207 ... after a concurrent reset dropped them"
#                -> introduced all three classifier-fix artifacts AND the .ts file as CRLF
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# NORMALIZED, exemption retired: ladder-recomputed.json (287 CRLF -> 287 LF, 11835 -> 11548
# bytes). EOL-ONLY PROOF: `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` empty over the change, and the parsed
# JSON object is identical pre/post. Its generator (ladder_recompute.py) now pins
# newline="\n", so a regeneration reproduces LF instead of re-dirtying the blob -- the
# exemption is retired and the source of the CRLF is closed in the same unit.
# NORMALIZED, exemptions retired: classifier-fix-delta.json (1775 CRLF -> LF, 69265 -> 67490
# bytes) and premise-audit-arrival-paths.json (5480 CRLF -> LF, 168210 -> 162730 bytes).
# EOL-ONLY PROOF for each: `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` empty over the change, and the parsed
# JSON object identical pre/post.
src/server/lib/spec-timeframe-recovery.ts                          !text !eol
